# rule.forbid.real-identities-in-fixtures

## .what
test code, fixtures, snapshots never carry a real person's name, email, or identity — the author's own included. use an obvious fake

## .why
fixtures + snapshots are committed and pushed; a real email ships to every clone forever. zero test value

## .how
- reuse the suite's extant placeholder (e.g. `Test Human` / `human@test.com`)
- a second identity → another obvious fake (`Jamie Rivera`, `jamie@example.com`)
- new emails use `@example.com` (rfc 2606)

## .enforcement
- real name or email in test code, fixture, or snapshot = blocker
- new fixture identity on a personal domain instead of `@example.com` = nitpick
